<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Every word the desktop app says. A language is a sibling folder: values-ru/strings.xml.
    Text that ketch serve sends, commands, tags, paths and the Ketch name are not here.

    Keys: <area>_<meaning>, one key per meaning: the looks share a key when they say the same thing, and the same English
    in two roles takes two keys (section_installed, status_installed), since other languages tell them apart.
    Values: %1$s and %1$d, numbered; a number that picks the wording makes it a plural.

    Terms, so that a translation says each the same way everywhere:
    package   what ketch installs: a CLI tool or an app
    source    where a package comes from: a GitHub repository or the registry
    pin       to keep a package at its version, by hand
    hold      what a pin or a ketch.lock does to a package: updates pass it by
    store     the folder that keeps the installed versions of a package
    link      to put a program from the store on PATH
-->
